# Cloudflare Pages response headers. Copied verbatim into dist/ by Vite.
#
# CSP lives here rather than in a <meta> tag so it applies to the deployed site only —
# a meta CSP would also hit `pnpm dev` and block Vite's HMR websocket.
#
# ## Why CSP is per-path and the hardening headers are not
#
# Cloudflare Pages *merges* every matching rule, and a browser given two
# `Content-Security-Policy` headers enforces the intersection — the most restrictive wins. So a
# `/embed/*` block granting `frame-ancestors *` underneath a `/*` block granting
# `frame-ancestors 'none'` does not loosen anything: the two are intersected and the embed stays
# blocked, while looking in the config exactly like it should work.
#
# The fix is that no path may match two blocks that both set CSP. The editor is a hash router,
# so every editor URL is literally `/` — which makes the document set small enough to enumerate:
# `/` and `/index.html` for the editor, `/p/*` and `/embed/*` for the viewer. CSP is set on
# those four and nowhere else.
#
# `/*` keeps the headers that are safe to apply everywhere and do not intersect destructively.
# COOP is listed there deliberately: it governs top-level browsing contexts only, so it is
# inert inside the embed's iframe and does not conflict with `frame-ancestors *`.
#
# Verify with `wrangler pages dev dist`, never `vite preview` — `vite preview` reads neither
# this file nor `_redirects`, which is how the `/view.html` rewrite bug stayed invisible.
/*
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()

# The editor. `connect-src` covers the AI relay (the browser's own Anthropic key goes through
# it) and the publication Worker (publish, update, unpublish). The two `sha256-` values cover
# the pre-paint theme scripts inlined in index.html and view.html; editing either invalidates
# its hash and the theme silently stops applying, so csp.test.ts recomputes both.
/
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'none'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' https://precipice-ai-proxy.precipice.workers.dev __PUBLICATION_API_ORIGIN__ https://challenges.cloudflare.com; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; script-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com 'sha256-Su/htfNLoOq1wMoi0QWMXhvrCg/hGbTFGjfv8xj3xtE=' 'sha256-nMDW8CM/K/J3ggYGmHQKHndwid1ilsGeb2eW3qjCyoo='

/index.html
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'none'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' https://precipice-ai-proxy.precipice.workers.dev __PUBLICATION_API_ORIGIN__ https://challenges.cloudflare.com; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; script-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com 'sha256-Su/htfNLoOq1wMoi0QWMXhvrCg/hGbTFGjfv8xj3xtE=' 'sha256-nMDW8CM/K/J3ggYGmHQKHndwid1ilsGeb2eW3qjCyoo='

# The public viewer. No AI relay in `connect-src`: this page has no key and makes no model call,
# and the narrower policy is what makes that a fact rather than an intention.
/p/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'none'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' __PUBLICATION_API_ORIGIN__; script-src 'self' 'sha256-Su/htfNLoOq1wMoi0QWMXhvrCg/hGbTFGjfv8xj3xtE=' 'sha256-nMDW8CM/K/J3ggYGmHQKHndwid1ilsGeb2eW3qjCyoo='

# The only block that permits framing, and the only one that may.
#
# `frame-ancestors *` is correct here because the embed is public, read-only, unauthenticated,
# and has no action to hijack — there is nothing for a clickjacker to make a victim click. That
# is a property of the bundle, not a promise: `src/viewer/bundle.test.ts` asserts the viewer
# ships no session token and no mutating call, and csp.test.ts asserts this is the only block
# that grants framing. If either stops being true, this line becomes a vulnerability.
/embed/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors *; form-action 'none'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' __PUBLICATION_API_ORIGIN__; script-src 'self' 'sha256-Su/htfNLoOq1wMoi0QWMXhvrCg/hGbTFGjfv8xj3xtE=' 'sha256-nMDW8CM/K/J3ggYGmHQKHndwid1ilsGeb2eW3qjCyoo='

# The service worker decides what every later request is allowed to use from cache, so a
# cached copy of it outlives any single deploy. Revalidating it on every load is what keeps a
# bad one from being permanent.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
